BT /F1 10.5 Tf 48.00 402.69 Td (Why these changes were done:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 382.52 Td (- @cap-js/sqlite is in dependencies, not devDependencies, because it must exist in the deployed Cloud) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 368.75 Td (Foundry app.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 352.98 Td (- @sap/cds is in dependencies because the deployed service needs CAP runtime.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 337.21 Td (- engines.node pins the intended Node.js major version for Cloud Foundry.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 321.44 Td (- start runs cds-deploy first so SQLite is initialized when the app starts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 305.67 Td (- cds.requires.db.kind = sqlite tells CAP to use SQLite.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 289.90 Td (- cds.requires.auth.kind = dummy avoids mandatory production authentication.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 48.00 274.13 Td (Impact:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 253.95 Td (- The CAP service can run in Cloud Foundry without HANA.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 238.18 Td (- No XSUAA service binding is required.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 222.41 Td (- No user login is required.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 60.00 206.64 Td (- The SQLite database is recreated or updated from deployment artifacts at startup.) Tj ET
